  "reasoning": "The defendant organized and mobilized villagers via mass text messages to gather at a construction site and physically block the work by climbing a tower crane, causing the project to be halted for months and resulting in significant economic loss. This conduct constitutes a group action that disrupts public order and the normal operation of a public construction site without legal authorization. Under Chinese criminal law, such behavior is charged as 聚众扰乱公共秩序罪 (crime of gathering a crowd to disturb public order). No evidence of property damage or other specific offenses (e.g., illegal assembly, robbery) is presented, so the appropriate charge is 聚众扰乱公共秩序罪.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]聚众扰乱公共秩序<eoa>"
}
